# Testing requirements

- Add or update tests before implementing behavior changes.
- Test success, failure and boundary conditions.
- Do not weaken assertions to make an implementation pass.
- Do not skip failing tests without explicit approval.
- Do not mock the main behavior being tested.
- Use deterministic local fixtures.
- Verify returned data and side effects, not only status codes.
- Security controls require negative tests proving that unsafe input is rejected.
- Run focused tests first, followed by the complete relevant suite.
